<name>Cylinder Block Assembly (2AZ-FE)</name>
<para id="RM00000224D000X" category="A" type-id="80002" name-id="070YD-00" from="200511">
<name>Disassembly</name>
<subpara id="RM00000224D000X_01" type-id="01" category="01">
<s-1 id="RM00000224D000X_01_0001" proc-id="E0505_____000004000000">
<ptxt>Inspect Connecting Rod Thrust Clearance</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<s2>
<ptxt>Using a dial indicator, measure the thrust clearance.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A036642J01" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<spec>
<subtitle>Standard</subtitle>
<specitem>
<ptxt>0.160-0.362mm</ptxt>
</specitem>
<subtitle>Limit</subtitle>
<specitem>
<ptxt>0.362mm</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
<atten4>
<ptxt>If the clearance is more than the maximum, replace the connecting rod and crankshaft.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</s2>
</content1>
</s-1>
<s-1 id="RM00000224D000X_01_0002" proc-id="E0505_____000004100000">
<ptxt>Inspect Connecting Rod Oil Clearance</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<s2>
<ptxt>Using paint, mark each connecting rod and cap with its cylinder number.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A063893J01" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<atten4>
<ptxt>This ensures correct reassembly of the connecting rods, caps and cylinders.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Using a socket wrench (12mm), remove the bolts and remove the bearing cap.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A013397J01" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Clean the inner and outer surfaces of the bearings, the connecting rod ends and the crank pins.</ptxt>
<atten3>
<ptxt>Check that there is no excessive wear or damage.</ptxt>
</atten3>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Lay a strip of Plastigage across the crank pin.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A036643J01" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Check the combination of the connecting rod and bearing cap and the front mark on the bearing cap, and assemble the bearing cap to the connecting rod.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A036691J01" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Apply a light coat of engine oil to the threads and seats of the bolts.</ptxt>
<atten3>
<ptxt>Tighten the connecting rod bolts using the plastic region tightening method.</ptxt>
</atten3>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Using a socket wrench (12mm), temporarily tighten the bolts in 2-3 steps, then tighten them to the specified torque.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A013397J01" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<torque>
<torqueitem>
<t-value1>25</t-value1>
<t-value2>250</t-value2>
</torqueitem>
</torque>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Mark the front of the bolt heads with paint.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A101478J01" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Using the paint marks as a guide, tighten each bolt an additional 90°.</ptxt>
<atten3>
<ptxt>Do not turn the crankshaft during measurement.</ptxt>
</atten3>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Remove the bearing caps and measure the Plastigage at its widest point.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A129453J01" width="2.775699831in" height="3.779676365in"/>
</figure>
<spec>
<subtitle>Standard</subtitle>
<specitem>
<ptxt>0.032-0.063mm</ptxt>
</specitem>
<subtitle>Limit</subtitle>
<specitem>
<ptxt>0.063mm</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
<atten3>
<ptxt>After inspection, completely remove the Plastigage.</ptxt>
</atten3>
<atten4>
<ptxt>If the clearance is more than the maximum, replace the bearings.</ptxt>
</atten4>
<table>
