<s-1 id="RM00000224D000X_01_0003" proc-id="E0505_____000004200000">
<ptxt>Remove Piston with Connecting Rod</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<s2>
<ptxt>Remove the 4 pistons with connecting rods from the cylinder block.</ptxt>
</s2>
</content1>
</s-1>
<s-1 id="RM00000224D000X_01_0004" proc-id="E0505_____000004300000">
<ptxt>Remove Connecting Rod Bearing</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<s2>
<ptxt>Remove the 8 connecting rod bearings from the connecting rods and bearing caps.</ptxt>
<atten4>
<ptxt>Arrange the removed parts in order according to their installation positions.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</s2>
</content1>
</s-1>
<s-1 id="RM00000224D000X_01_0005" proc-id="E0505_____000004400000">
<ptxt>Remove Piston Ring Set</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<s2>
<ptxt>Using a piston ring expander, remove the compression ring No.1 and compression ring No.2.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A128232" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Remove the oil ring expander and oil ring by hand.</ptxt>
</s2>
</content1>
</s-1>
<s-1 id="RM00000224D000X_01_0006" proc-id="E0505_____000004500000">
<ptxt>Remove Piston Pin Hole Snap Ring</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<s2>
<ptxt>Using a small screwdriver, remove the snap ring.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A128233" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
</s2>
</content1>
</s-1>
<s-1 id="RM00000224D000X_01_0007" proc-id="E0505_____000004600000">
<ptxt>Remove Piston</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<s2>
<ptxt>Heat the piston to approximately 80°C.</ptxt>
<atten2>
<ptxt>The piston is hot, so always wear gloves when working.</ptxt>
</atten2>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Push out the piston pin with your thumb and remove it from the piston.</ptxt>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Arrange the removed parts in order according to their installation positions.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A128239J01" width="2.775699831in" height="3.779676365in"/>
</figure>
<atten3>
<ptxt>The selection mark for the pin hole diameter is stamped at the position shown in the illustration, but no selection mark is stamped on the piston pin, so do not change its combination with the piston.</ptxt>
</atten3>
</s2>
</content1>
</s-1>
<s-1 id="RM00000224D000X_01_0008" proc-id="E0505_____000004700000">
<ptxt>Inspect Crankshaft Thrust Clearance</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<s2>
<ptxt>Using a dial indicator and a screwdriver, measure the thrust clearance.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A128234" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<spec>
<subtitle>Standard</subtitle>
<specitem>
<ptxt>0.04-0.24mm</ptxt>
</specitem>
<subtitle>Limit</subtitle>
<specitem>
<ptxt>0.30mm</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
<atten4>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>If the clearance is more than the maximum, replace the thrust washers or crankshaft.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Thrust Washer Thickness 1.930-1.980mm</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten4>
</s2>
</content1>
</s-1>
<s-1 id="RM00000224D000X_01_0009" proc-id="E0505_____000004800000">
<ptxt>Remove Crankshaft</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<s2>
<ptxt>Uniformly loosen the bearing cap bolts in 2-3 steps in the order shown in the illustration, and remove the 10 bearing cap bolts.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A128235J01" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Remove the 5 bearing caps and remove the crankshaft.</ptxt>
</s2>
</content1>
</s-1>
<s-1 id="RM00000224D000X_01_0010" proc-id="E0505_____000004900000">
<ptxt>Remove Crankshaft Thrust Washer Upper</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<s2>
<ptxt>Remove the crankshaft thrust washer set from the front and rear of the No. No.3 journal on the cylinder block.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A013501J01" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
</s2>
</content1>
</s-1>
<s-1 id="RM00000224D000X_01_0011" proc-id="E0505_____000004A00000">
<ptxt>Remove Crankshaft Bearing</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<s2>
<ptxt>Remove the 5 crankshaft bearings from the cylinder block.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A063901J01" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<atten4>
<ptxt>Arrange the removed parts in order according to their installation positions.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</s2>
</content1>
</s-1>
<s-1 id="RM00000224D000X_01_0012" proc-id="E0505_____000004B00000">
<ptxt>Remove Crankshaft Bearing NO.2</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<s2>
<ptxt>Remove the 5 crankshaft bearings No.2 from the bearing caps.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A063902J01" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<atten4>
<ptxt>Arrange the removed parts in order according to their installation positions.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</s2>
</content1>
</s-1>
<s-1 id="RM00000224D000X_01_0013" proc-id="E0505_____000004C00000">
<ptxt>Remove Oil Nozzle Sub-assembly NO.1</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<s2>
<ptxt>Using a 5 socket hexagon wrench, remove the 4 oil nozzles No.1.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A128251J01" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
</s2>
</content1>
</s-1>
<s-1 id="RM00000224D000X_01_0014" proc-id="E0505_____000004D00000">
<ptxt>Inspect Oil Nozzle Sub-assembly NO.1</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<s2>
<ptxt>Inspect the oil nozzles for damage or clogging.</ptxt>
<atten4>
<ptxt>If there is damage or clogging, replace the oil nozzle.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</s2>
</content1>
</s-1>
<s-1 id="RM00000224D000X_01_0015" proc-id="E0505_____000007P00000">
<ptxt>Remove Stud Bolt</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<s2>
<ptxt>Remove the stud bolts from the cylinder block.</ptxt>
</s2>
</content1>
</s-1>
<s-1 id="RM00000224D000X_01_0026" proc-id="E0505_____00000DR00000">
<ptxt>Remove Ring Pin</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<s2>
<ptxt>Remove the ring pins from the cylinder block.</ptxt>
</s2>
</content1>
</s-1>
<s-1 id="RM00000224D000X_01_0028" proc-id="E0505_____00000DS00000">
<ptxt>Remove Straight Pin</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<s2>
<ptxt>Remove the straight pins from the cylinder block.</ptxt>
</s2>
</content1>
</s-1>
<s-1 id="RM00000224D000X_01_0016" proc-id="E0505_____000004E00000">
<ptxt>Inspect Cylinder Block for Warpage</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<s2>
<ptxt>Using a precision straightedge and feeler gauge, measure the warpage of the top surface of the cylinder block.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A036648J01" width="2.775699831in" height="3.779676365in"/>
</figure>
<spec>
<subtitle>Limit</subtitle>
<specitem>
<ptxt>0.05mm</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
<atten4>
<ptxt>If the warpage is more than the maximum, replace the cylinder block.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</s2>
</content1>
</s-1>
<s-1 id="RM00000224D000X_01_0017" proc-id="E0505_____000004F00000">
<ptxt>Inspect Cylinder Bore</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<s2>
<ptxt>Using a cylinder gauge, measure the bore diameter at the 4 positions shown in the illustration.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A091964J01" width="2.775699831in" height="3.779676365in"/>
</figure>
<spec>
<subtitle>Standard</subtitle>
<specitem>
<ptxt>88.500-88.513mm</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
<spec>
<title>Limit</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>88.633mm</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
<atten4>
<ptxt>If the warpage is more than the maximum, replace the cylinder block.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</s2>
</content1>
</s-1>
<s-1 id="RM00000224D000X_01_0018" proc-id="E0505_____000004G00000">
<ptxt>Inspect Piston Outer Diameter</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<s2>
<ptxt>Using a micrometer, measure the piston diameter at right angles to the piston pin hole, 44.3mm from the top of the piston.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A128236J01" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<spec>
<subtitle>Standard</subtitle>
<specitem>
<ptxt>88.469-88.479mm</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
</s2>
</content1>
</s-1>
<s-1 id="RM00000224D000X_01_0019" proc-id="E0505_____000004H00000">
<ptxt>Inspect Piston Clearance</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<s2>
<ptxt>Calculate the clearance from the minimum cylinder bore diameter and the piston diameter.</ptxt>
<spec>
<subtitle>Standard</subtitle>
<specitem>
<ptxt>0.021-0.044mm</ptxt>
</specitem>
<subtitle>Limit</subtitle>
<specitem>
<ptxt>0.1mm</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
<atten4>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>If the clearance is more than the maximum, replace the piston or cylinder block.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Oil clearance = minimum cylinder bore diameter - piston diameter.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten4>
</s2>
</content1>
</s-1>
<s-1 id="RM00000224D000X_01_0020" proc-id="E0505_____000004I00000">
<ptxt>Inspect Ring Groove Clearance</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<s2>
<ptxt>Using a feeler gauge, measure the clearance between the piston ring and the ring groove around the entire circumference of the piston.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A128237" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<spec>
<title>Standard</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="2">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.07in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="2.06in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry>
<ptxt>Type</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry>
<ptxt>Standard [mm]</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry>
<ptxt>No. No.1 Ring</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry>
<ptxt>0.02-0.07</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<ptxt>No. No.2 Ring</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry>
<ptxt>0.02-0.06</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<ptxt>Oil Ring</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry>
<ptxt>0.02-0.07</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</s2>
</content1>
</s-1>
<s-1 id="RM00000224D000X_01_0021" proc-id="E0505_____000004J00000">
<ptxt>Inspect Piston Ring End Gap</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<s2>
<ptxt>Using a piston, push the piston ring approximately 110mm down from the top of the cylinder block.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A032399J01" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Using a feeler gauge, measure the end gap of the piston ring.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="EM02552J01" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<spec>
<subtitle>Standard</subtitle>
<specitem>
<ptxt/>
</specitem>
<table frame="all" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
<tgroup cols="3" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
<colspec colnum="01" colname="C01" colwidth="1.395267     in"/>
<colspec colnum="02" colname="C02" colwidth="1.395268     in"/>
<colspec colnum="03" colname="C03" colwidth="1.395267     in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry colname="C01" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Ring</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname="C02" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Standard [mm]</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname="C03" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Maximum [mm]</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry colname="C01" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>No.1</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname="C02" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>0.24-0.31</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname="C03" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>0.89</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry colname="C01" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>No.2</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname="C02" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>0.33-0.43</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname="C03" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>1.37</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry colname="C01" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Oil</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname="C02" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>0.10-0.30</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname="C03" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>0.73</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
<atten4>
<ptxt>If the end gap is more than the maximum, replace the piston ring set.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</s2>
</content1>
</s-1>
<s-1 id="RM00000224D000X_01_0022" proc-id="E0505_____000004K00000">
<ptxt>Inspect Piston Pin Oil Clearance</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<s2>
<ptxt>Using a caliper gauge, measure the inside diameter of the piston pin hole.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A128238" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<spec>
<subtitle>Standard</subtitle>
<specitem>
<ptxt>22.001-22.010mm</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Using a micrometer, measure the piston pin diameter.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A120741J02" width="2.775699831in" height="2.775699831in"/>
</figure>
<spec>
<subtitle>Standard</subtitle>
<specitem>
<ptxt>21.997-22.006mm</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Calculate the clearance from the piston pin hole inside diameter and the piston pin diameter.</ptxt>
<spec>
<subtitle>Standard</subtitle>
<specitem>
<ptxt>0.001-0.007mm</ptxt>
</specitem>
<subtitle>Limit</subtitle>
<specitem>
<ptxt>0.010mm</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
<atten4>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Oil clearance = piston pin hole inside diameter - piston pin diameter.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>If the clearance is more than the maximum, replace the piston with pin. </ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten4>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Using a caliper gauge, measure the inside diameter of the connecting rod small end bushing.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A001185J01" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<spec>
<subtitle>Standard</subtitle>
<specitem>
<ptxt>22.005-22.014mm</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Calculate the clearance from the connecting rod small end bore diameter and the piston pin diameter.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A128239J01" width="2.775699831in" height="3.779676365in"/>
</figure>
<spec>
<subtitle>Standard</subtitle>
<specitem>
<ptxt>0.005-0.011mm</ptxt>
</specitem>
<subtitle>Limit</subtitle>
<specitem>
<ptxt>0.011mm</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
<atten3>
<ptxt>The selection mark for the pin hole diameter is stamped at the position shown in the illustration, but no selection mark is stamped on the piston pin, so do not change its combination with the piston.</ptxt>
</atten3>
<atten4>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>If the clearance is more than the maximum, replace the piston with pin or the connecting rod.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Oil clearance = connecting rod bore inside diameter - piston pin diameter.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten4>
